From 5a33ff8a3daea75b55335e52dde15382f550a0a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TAKANO Mitsuhiro <takano32@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:17:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] arm64: errata: Mark GIC-700 #2941627 N/A in
 silicon-errata

The GIC-700 #2941627 entry in the arm64 silicon-errata table names
ARM64_ERRATUM_2941627 in its Kconfig column, but no Kconfig file defines
that symbol and no code refers to it.  A reader who goes from the table
to the option finds nothing on the other end, which is the dead end this
table exists to prevent.

The workaround for this erratum does not need a symbol: irq-gic-v3.c
hands GICD_IIDR to gic_enable_quirks(), which matches it against its
quirk table, and gic_enable_quirk_arm64_2941627() enables a static
branch.  The table already records workarounds of that kind as "N/A",
for example NVIDIA T241-FABRIC-4, which is also a GIC quirk.

Set the Kconfig column to "N/A" to match those entries.

Only the text of the table changes, and no build was run.

Fixes: 6fe5c68ee6a1 ("irqchip/gic-v3: Workaround for GIC-700 erratum 2941627")
---
 Documentation/arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst b/Documentation/arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst
index afe109afe692..afea5e57ab95 100644
--- a/Documentation/arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst
+++ b/Documentation/arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst
@@ -279,7 +279,7 @@ stable kernels.
 | ARM            | MMU S3          | #3995052,       | N/A                         |
 |                |                 | #3673557        |                             |
 +----------------+-----------------+-----------------+-----------------------------+
-| ARM            | GIC-700         | #2941627        | ARM64_ERRATUM_2941627       |
+| ARM            | GIC-700         | #2941627        | N/A                         |
 +----------------+-----------------+-----------------+-----------------------------+
 | ARM            | SI L1           | #4311569        | ARM64_ERRATUM_4311569       |
 +----------------+-----------------+-----------------+-----------------------------+
